</name><name><surname>Chapman</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The pharmacology of excitatory and inhibitory amino acid-mediated events in the transmission and modulation of pain in the spinal cord</article-title><source>Gen Pharmacol</source><year>1997</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>633</fpage><lpage>638</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9184794</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garry</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fleetwood-Walker</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A new view on how AMPA receptors and their interacting proteins mediate neuropathic pain</article-title><source>Pain</source><year>2004</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>210</fpage><lpage>213</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15157680</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pain.2004.04.002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Furuyama</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiyama</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Sato</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>HT</given-names></name><name><surname>Maeno</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Takagi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tohyama</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Region-specific expression of subunits of ionotropic glutamate receptors (AMPA-type, KA-type and NMDA receptors) in the rat spinal cord with special reference to nociception</article-title><source>Brain Res Mol Brain Res</source><year>1993</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>141</fpage><lpage>151</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8097549</pub-id><pub-id pub-